        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Black silk embroidery on white cotton, Leksand, Dalarna, 1840"@en , "Square piece of white cotton, three corners are embroidered with satin and cross stitch in black silk, square patterns and connected by geometrical borders and sprigs. Signed ' A K D' and dated '1840'. There are tassels at the four corners."@en , "The neckerchief was worn folded (that is why only three corners are embroidered, the fourth would have been hidden) on formal occasions. This specific embroidery technique is called \"svartstick\" in Sweden (blackstitch)."@en ;
